Notre groupe gère actuellement 3 garages et une carrosserie, situés aux Acacias et au Grand-Pré, où nous proposons les marques Jaguar, Land Rover, Volvo et Morgan, ainsi que des services après-vente, des magasins de pièces détachées et d-accessoires d-origine. Entreprise familiale et indépendante crée en 1968, nous nous développons grâce aux compétences et à l-engagement de notre centaine de collaboratrices et collaborateurs, en restant fidèles à nos valeurs.
Afin de soutenir le développement de nos activités, nous recherchons un.e
**Conseiller.ère de Vente Automobile (100%)**
**Activités principales:**
* Vente de véhicules neufs et d'occasion;
* Maîtriser et proposer différents types de financement;
* Préparer et suivre les dossiers de la création du lead jusqu'à la livraison du véhicule;
* Prospecter le marché régional (société et privé);
* Développer et fidéliser votre portefeuille client;
* Veiller à la satisfaction des clients;
* Contribuer à maintenir un niveau de service conforme aux standards de marques de luxe et premium et que nous représentons.
**Votre profil**
* Vous savez négocier de manière professionnelle avec une clientèle VIP exigeante et internationale;
* Vous justifiez d'une expérience confirmée dans le domaine automobile ou le commerce de produits similaires;
* Maîtrise du français et **anglais C1** minimum exigé;
* Capacité à gérer plusieurs dossiers en parallèle avec rigueur et organisation;
* Bonne maîtrise des outils informatiques et des logiciels métiers liés à l-automobile;
* Présentation irréprochable, attitude professionnelle et orientée solutions;
* Flexibilité, proactivité et forte capacité à travailler en équipe;
Entrée en fonction : immédiate
**Seuls les dossiers complets (CV, Lettre de motivation, Certificats) postés sur JoubUp seront pris en considération.**

Based in our dynamic office in Hamburg, you will join our growing team of Sales Representatives that are playing a crucial role in Flexport European growth plans. Strategically and with a lot of creativity you will be tasked to getting in touch with good fit companies that want to engage in a conversation with Flexport.
No two days will be the same in this challenging role where you will be responsible for:
Identify and create new sales opportunities for Flexport Europe;
Working with Account Executives all over Europe to identify and prioritize strategic opportunities;
Demonstrating the value of our offering through phone calls, email, and other social mediums;
This role will give you the opportunity to learn how global trade works from the ground up and build the foundation for your career in tech sales. Shadowing Account Executives in meetings and other activities to help you acquire the skills you’ll need for your next role on the Flexport sales team.

This is an excellent opportunity to join a dynamic team in a business that is going to coach and develop you. We view our sales development teams as the talent engine for the rest of the sales organisation. Meaning: we give you the tools to be empowered and really take your sales and consultative skills to the next level.
You’ll be joining a sales team with a lot of emphasis, combining great culture, a place to succeed and focus on career development make this a fun & dynamic place to work.

* Assisting in the strategic development and implementation of large-scale transformation projects in the Life Science industry;
* Assisting with facilitating workshops and discussions with stakeholders;
* Collaborating with the team to analyse data, develop compelling visualizations and create effective and engaging presentations for clients;
* Developing storylines that effectively communicate complex concepts to a non-technical audience;
* Working closely with your colleagues to ensure data accuracy, completeness, and quality;
* Continuously evaluating and improving presentation and storyline effectiveness based on client feedback;
* Actively participating in business development activities within the team.
* Knowing how to incorporate AI in your day-to-day workflows without compromising quality

* Be the change by supporting our clients through innovative strategy projects around digital, future-proof topics that challenge and transform the status quo;
* Craft your own career path through continuous learning and personal growth;
* Experience the benefits of hybrid working, offering flexibility and ensuring work-life balance, 5 weeks of vacation, employee referral bonus, company shares program and annual contribution to a fitness subscription;
* We believe that Diversity & Inclusion are our greatest strengths - our long-standing corporate culture is open-minded and internationally oriented.
Capgemini Switzerland is an equal opportunity employer. We promote equality and dignity in all aspects of recruitment and employment, and all offers of employment and promotions are made on the basis of performance, competence and ability.
Our Life Sciences team is dedicated to helping Pharma and MedTech organizations break through barriers to deliver better patient outcomes. In a world where data, AI, and patient expectations are rapidly evolving, we bring integrated thinking that connects business, technology, and human insight. We understand that innovation happens where empathy meets engineering - where strategy, science, and digital transformation align.
With a proven track record across 40+ countries, we partner with clients from strategy to implementation, enabling them to lead the next generation of health. Whether it's reimagining patient experience, accelerating research and Development (R&D), or building sustainable, data-driven operations - our team is here to help you move faster, smarter, and with purpose.
